content.text:
1→{
  "attempt_id": "ATT-0136",
  "campaign_id": "C66-001",
  "campaign_revision": 6,
  "checked_claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "CLM-0136-1",
      "note": "Lowest-weight surjection W_k H^k(C^n) ->> W_k H^k(M_{g,n}). Reconstructed independently: M_{6,6} is the complement of the pairwise diagonals in C^6, hence open dense, so any smooth proper DM compactification Y of C^6 is simultaneously one of M_{6,6}; by Deligne Hodge II 3.2.17 both lowest-weight groups equal im(H^k(Y)->-), and restriction factors that common image. Only the containment direction is used, so the kernel, Gysin exactness for diagonals, and Schur-Weyl are genuinely not invoked. Matches FND-0197 verbatim in scope, including the explicit exclusion of the non-proper f:M_{g,n}->M_g whose R^1 is mixed (FND-0020, FND-0037).",
      "verdict": "confirmed"
10→    },
    {
      "claim_id": "CLM-0136-2",
      "note": "C^6 -> M_6 is smooth and proper (fibre product of the closed universal curve), R^j pi_* Q concentrated in j=0,1,2, relative Kunneth gives R^q f_* Q = sum_{|i|=q} tensor_s R^{i_s}. The MHS-level splitting (not merely a degeneration of the associated graded) is supplied by the relative Chow-Kunneth projectors, which are algebraic correspondences and hence MHS morphisms, so W_k is additive over the summands. Weight bookkeeping checks: tensor_s R^{i_s} has weight |i|, H^{k-|i|}(M_g;L_{|i|}) has weights >= k, so W_k is its lowest-weight piece in every summand. Note: the displayed expression pi_2 = psi_2/(2g-2) - kappa_1/(2(2g-2)^2) is written as a class on the curve rather than as a correspondence on C x_{M_g} C; it is reproduced verbatim from FND-0196(2) and is used only in Disposal B, which the theorem does not need (Disposal A alone closes the step), so this shorthand is not load-bearing.",
      "verdict": "confirmed"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "CLM-0136-3",
      "note": "Kunneth inhomogeneity of omega_s = a_s + b_s + c_s is exactly FND-0196, and the attempt states it as a used step rather than a repair. Disposal A verified independently: H^2(M_{g,1};Q) has rank 2 with basis {lambda, omega} for g>=3, forcing the H^1(M_g;V) Leray graded piece of H^2(C) to vanish, which is the rational form of Morita's H_1(Mod_g;H_1(Sigma_g;Z)) = Z/(2g-2); hence b_s = 0 for g=6. Also verified that a_s lies in W_2 H^2(M_g) (H^2(M_6;Q)=Q.lambda, algebraic of type (1,1)) and that b_s would lie in W_2 H^1(M_g;V), so both cross terms land in the correct W_26 summands of the corresponding multi-indices.",
      "verdict": "confirmed"
20→    },
